{"body": "The amounts under clause (i), (ii), or (iii) (whichever is applicable) of subparagraph (A) shall be reduced (but not below zero) by the amount of wages taken into account in determining the tax imposed under section 3121(b)(2) with respect to the taxpayer.", "citation_label": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 1401(b)(2)(B)", "citation_path": "us/statute/26/1401/b/2/B", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2026-07-12", "heading": "Coordination with FICA", "id": "90e0fe29-e708-55c2-af18-37749e2195ad", "identifiers": {"usc:paragraph": "2", "usc:section": "1401", "usc:subparagraph": "B", "usc:subsection": "b", "usc:title": "26", "uslm:identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s1401/b/2/B"}, "jurisdiction": "us", "kind": "subparagraph", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 1401(b)(2)(B)", "level": 4, "metadata": {"created_date": "2026-04-17", "heading": "Coordination with FICA", "identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s1401/b/2/B", "kind": "subparagraph", "paragraph": "2", "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26/1401/b/2", "publication_name": "Online@119-102", "references_to": [], "section": "1401", "section_heading": "Rate of tax", "source_download_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/102not101/xml_usc26@119-102not101.zip", "subparagraph": "B", "subsection": "b", "title": "26", "title_heading": "INTERNAL REVENUE CODE"}, "ordinal": 14010002002002, "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26/1401/b/2", "parent_id": "92076c6c-15e2-57c4-8cda-e4520eef7a3c", "source_as_of": "2026-07-12", "source_format": "uslm-xml", "source_id": "/us/usc/t26/s1401/b/2/B", "source_path": "sources/us/statute/2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26/uslm/usc26.xml", "source_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title26-section1401&num=0&edition=prelim", "version": "2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26"}
{"body": "During any period in which there is in effect an agreement entered into pursuant to section 233 of the Social Security Act with any foreign country, the self-employment income of an individual shall be exempt from the taxes imposed by this section to the extent that such self-employment income is subject under such agreement exclusively to the laws applicable to the social security system of such foreign country.", "citation_label": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 1401(c)", "citation_path": "us/statute/26/1401/c", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2026-07-12", "heading": "Relief from taxes in cases covered by certain international agreements", "id": "227e5f38-66e7-526e-8a57-48930f48d018", "identifiers": {"usc:section": "1401", "usc:subsection": "c", "usc:title": "26", "uslm:identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s1401/c"}, "jurisdiction": "us", "kind": "subsection", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 1401(c)", "level": 2, "metadata": {"created_date": "2026-04-17", "heading": "Relief from taxes in cases covered by certain international agreements", "identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s1401/c", "kind": "subsection", "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26/1401", "publication_name": "Online@119-102", "references_to": [], "section": "1401", "section_heading": "Rate of tax", "source_download_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/102not101/xml_usc26@119-102not101.zip", "subsection": "c", "title": "26", "title_heading": "INTERNAL REVENUE CODE"}, "ordinal": 14010003, "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26/1401", "parent_id": "e4f22eb8-941e-56ef-944e-36a880ec5a1f", "source_as_of": "2026-07-12", "source_format": "uslm-xml", "source_id": "/us/usc/t26/s1401/c", "source_path": "sources/us/statute/2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26/uslm/usc26.xml", "source_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title26-section1401&num=0&edition=prelim", "version": "2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26"}
{"body": "(a) Old-age, survivors, and disability insurance In addition to other taxes, there is hereby imposed on the income of every individual a tax equal to 6.2 percent of the wages (as defined in section 3121(a)) received by the individual with respect to employment (as defined in section 3121(b)).\n\n(b) Hospital insurance (1) In general In addition to the tax imposed by the preceding subsection, there is hereby imposed on the income of every individual a tax equal to 1.45 percent of the wages (as defined in section 3121(a)) received by him with respect to employment (as defined in section 3121(b)). (2) Additional tax In addition to the tax imposed by paragraph (1) and the preceding subsection, there is hereby imposed on every taxpayer (other than a corporation, estate, or trust) a tax equal to 0.9 percent of wages which are received with respect to employment (as defined in section 3121(b)) during any taxable year beginning after December 31, 2012 , and which are in excess of\u2014 (A) in the case of a joint return, $250,000, (B) in the case of a married taxpayer (as defined in section 7703) filing a separate return, \u00bd of the dollar amount determined under subparagraph (A), and (C) in any other case, $200,000.\n\n(c) Relief from taxes in cases covered by certain international agreements During any period in which there is in effect an agreement entered into pursuant to section 233 of the Social Security Act with any foreign country, wages received by or paid to an individual shall be exempt from the taxes imposed by this section to the extent that such wages are subject under such agreement exclusively to the laws applicable to the social security system of such foreign country.", "citation_label": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 3101", "citation_path": "us/statute/26/3101", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2026-07-12", "heading": "Rate of tax", "id": "a0e0112b-9ca1-57e0-9a5d-7c9062cb1eeb", "identifiers": {"usc:section": "3101", "usc:title": "26", "uslm:identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s3101"}, "jurisdiction": "us", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 3101", "level": 1, "metadata": {"created_date": "2026-04-17", "heading": "Rate of tax", "identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s3101", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26", "publication_name": "Online@119-102", "references_to": ["us/statute/26/1", "us/statute/26/1401", "us/statute/26/164", "us/statute/26/3101", "us/statute/26/3111", "us/statute/26/3121", "us/statute/42/1395i\u20131", "us/statute/42/409", "us/statute/42/433"], "section": "3101", "source_download_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/102not101/xml_usc26@119-102not101.zip", "title": "26", "title_heading": "INTERNAL REVENUE CODE"}, "ordinal": 31010, "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26", "parent_id": "e61132a5-5a54-54b1-9cd8-ac126c3260c8", "source_as_of": "2026-07-12", "source_format": "uslm-xml", "source_id": "/us/usc/t26/s3101", "source_path": "sources/us/statute/2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26/uslm/usc26.xml", "source_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title26-section3101&num=0&edition=prelim", "version": "2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26"}
{"body": "In addition to other taxes, there is hereby imposed on the income of every individual a tax equal to 6.2 percent of the wages (as defined in section 3121(a)) received by the individual with respect to employment (as defined in section 3121(b)).", "citation_label": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 3101(a)", "citation_path": "us/statute/26/3101/a", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2026-07-12", "heading": "Old-age, survivors, and disability insurance", "id": "ee7540b2-21e9-50f6-b5a2-3ba2712197b5", "identifiers": {"usc:section": "3101", "usc:subsection": "a", "usc:title": "26", "uslm:identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s3101/a"}, "jurisdiction": "us", "kind": "subsection", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "26 U.S.C. \u00a7 3101(a)", "level": 2, "metadata": {"created_date": "2026-04-17", "heading": "Old-age, survivors, and disability insurance", "identifier": "/us/usc/t26/s3101/a", "kind": "subsection", "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26/3101", "publication_name": "Online@119-102", "references_to": [], "section": "3101", "section_heading": "Rate of tax", "source_download_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/102not101/xml_usc26@119-102not101.zip", "subsection": "a", "title": "26", "title_heading": "INTERNAL REVENUE CODE"}, "ordinal": 31010001, "parent_citation_path": "us/statute/26/3101", "parent_id": "a0e0112b-9ca1-57e0-9a5d-7c9062cb1eeb", "source_as_of": "2026-07-12", "source_format": "uslm-xml", "source_id": "/us/usc/t26/s3101/a", "source_path": "sources/us/statute/2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26/uslm/usc26.xml", "source_url": "https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title26-section3101&num=0&edition=prelim", "version": "2026-07-24-1401-coordination-repair-title-26"}
